<ChartsRuntimeNotice />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartBasicExample" Title="Line chart with legend and tooltip" Description="Start with an NTChart and one series per measure. Give the chart a height, because it fills its parent, and add NTLegend and NTTooltip so readers can tell the series apart and read exact values." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartTitleExample" Title="Chart title" Description="TitleOptions names the chart inside the canvas, so the title also appears in exported PNGs. Use it when the chart is shared or exported on its own." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartCategoryAxisExample" Title="Category axis with axis titles" Description="String X values make a category axis. NTXAxisOptions and NTYAxisOptions add axis titles, and LabelFormat shows units on the value axis." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartNumericAxisExample" Title="Numeric axis" Description="Numeric X values place points by value rather than evenly by category. Use it for measurements taken at uneven intervals." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartDateTimeAxisExample" Title="Date axis" Description="DateTime X values give a time axis with date-aware ticks. Use it for time series so gaps between dates stay proportional." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartSecondaryAxisExample" Title="Secondary Y axis" Description="Register a second NTYAxisOptions and set UseSecondaryYAxis on a series to plot measures with different units, such as revenue and units sold, in one chart." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartLegendExample" Title="Legend position" Description="Position places the legend at the top, bottom, left or right, or floats it over the plot. Move it to the side when the chart is short and wide." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartLegendScrollExample" Title="Legend with many items" Description="A legend never pushes the plot off the canvas. Top and bottom legends show at most MaxRows rows and scroll sideways; left, right and floating legends scroll up and down. Scroll with the mouse wheel over the legend." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartLongLabelsExample" Title="Long axis labels" Description="Long category names wrap onto two lines when there is room. When the columns are too narrow they are rotated and shortened to MaxLabelWidth with an ellipsis; hover a shortened label to read it in full. Set MaxLabelWidth to null to always draw labels in full." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartAnnotationsExample" Title="Annotations" Description="Annotations mark targets, ranges and events on the plot. Use them to give the data context, such as a goal line or a promotion period." />
<DocsExample TExample="ChartInteractionsExample" Title="Pan, zoom, reset, export and click" Description="Interactions enables pan and zoom on a series, which also shows the reset button. The chart's export button saves a PNG, and OnClick reports the clicked data point." />
